❗️<b>State Social Scholarship (SSS)</b>

📎<b>Mode of Study:</b> full-time, state-funded.

📎<b>Academic Performance: </b>regardless of academic performance.

📎<b>Citizenship: </b>Russian Federation

📎<b>Categories for social scholarship:</b>
✨ orphans and children left without parental care (including persons from among them);
✨ those who have lost both parents or a sole parent during the period of study;
✨ disabled children, disabled persons of groups I and II, disabled since childhood;
✨ those affected by radiation (Chernobyl, other radiation disasters, Semipalatinsk test site);
✨ disabled due to military injury or disease contracted during service, and combat veterans;
✨ those who have served under contract for at least 3 years in positions of soldiers/sergeants and were discharged on certain grounds;
✨ those who have received state social assistance.

❗️<b>Amount:</b>

3️⃣6️⃣2️⃣9️⃣<i> ₽ per month.</i>

✨ Bachelor's, specialist, and master's students.

📎<b>To receive the scholarship, the student submits to the Dean's Office:</b>

✨ an application addressed to the Rector (Director of the branch) requesting the appointment of the SSS;
✨ a document membership in one of the categories.

❗️The SSS is awarded to the student from the date of submission of the supporting document.

❗️<b>Students have the right to:</b>
✨ receive education and participate in shaping its content;
✨ study according to an individual plan, choose elective courses;
✨ respect for dignity, protection from violence, freedom of conscience and information;
✨ holidays, academic leave, maternity leave, and childcare leave;
✨ transfer, reinstatement, transition from fee-paying to state-funded education;
✨ participate in the management of the university, appeal against acts;
✨ free use of the library, infrastructure, and sports facilities;
✨ development of creative abilities, participation in competitions, olympiads, and research activities;
✨ free publication of works in university publications;
✨ incentives for achievements, receipt of scholarships and financial assistance;
✨ provision of accommodation in the dormitory subject to availability;
✨ deferment from military conscription.

❗️<b>Students are obliged to:</b>
✨ conscientiously master the programme, attend classes, and complete assignments;
✨ resume studies after academic leave, maternity leave, or quarantine;
✨comply with the Charter, Code of Ethics, Dormitory Rules, and these Rules;
✨ take care of their health, respect the honour and dignity of others;
✨ not use violence, not insult others;
✨ promptly notify about absences and provide supporting documents;
✨ have their campus card with them, observe the business dress code;
✨ not use unauthorised aids during assessments;
✨ take care of property, compensate for damage;
✨ maintain cleanliness and order, observe discipline during classes;
✨ report suspicious requests, not conduct political agitation;
✨ not share logins and passwords, not distribute educational materials;
✨ not create obstacles to the educational process;
✨ not submit forged documents, comply with information security requirements.

📎<b>International students</b> are additionally obliged to comply with the migration legislation of the Russian Federation.

❗️<b>Prohibited:</b>
✨ smoking (including vapes);
✨ use of scented candles and lamps;
✨ consumption of alcohol and drugs, being under the influence;
✨ violation of access control and fire safety regulations;
✨ removal of property without permission;
✨ use of equipment for personal purposes;
✨ creating noise, talking, using gadgets during classes;
✨ being in outerwear and headwear;
✨ eating in classrooms;
✨ posting announcements and inscriptions without permission;
✨ gambling, profanity;
✨ parking vehicles and scooters without permission.

❗️<b>Liabilities:</b>

✨ Penalties: reprimand, severe reprimand, expulsion (for violation of the Charter, Rules, Code of Ethics, etc.).

❗️ One penalty per offence. The severity, circumstances, conduct, and condition are taken into account.

📎 Not applied: during illness, holidays, academic leave, maternity leave; to students with mental retardation and intellectual disabilities.

📎 Before a penalty — written notice, explanation within 3️⃣ academic days (university) or 3️⃣ working days (schools/SPO). Refusal to give an explanation does not prevent the imposition.

📎 Time limit: no later than 1️⃣ month from discovery, but no later than 6️⃣ months from commission.

📎 Expulsion of minors (from 1️⃣5️⃣ years) — only for repeated offences, if other measures have failed. Requires consideration of the opinion of the student council and parents; for those who have not received basic general education — consent of the commission on minors' affairs; for orphans — consent of guardianship authorities.

📎 The order is communicated to the student/parents within 3️⃣ academic days.

✨ The penalty is valid for 1️⃣ year. If no new penalty is imposed during the year, it is considered lifted. May be lifted early.

🔍During the period of a penalty, incentives are not applied. A penalty is grounds for cancellation of the tuition fee discount.

🔍The Accommodation Services Office is a department that ensures the check-in of non-resident students and event participants, the rational use of dormitory space, and the monitoring of residence.

📎<b>Functions of the department:</b>
✨ provision of places in accordance with legislation and local regulations;
✨ monitoring of available places and distribution of students by faculty and duration of study;
✨ execution of tenancy agreements, registration, terminations, and military records;
✨ monitoring of payments and arrears;
✨ preparation of check-in schedules and placement lists for the hotel-type dormitory;
✨ preparation of reports, maintenance of contracts for events;
✨ monitoring of accommodation costs and formation of price lists.

❗️The Office is located at: Moscow, 10 Baltiyskaya Street, Building 3, basement floor.

